  "ENSEMBLE_EQUAL is mechanically identical to the frozen primary comparator (same members, equal weights, same mixture), so relative loss = 1.0 exactly; an ensemble of comparator members cannot pass C1 (threshold 0.97)",
  "INVERSE_MSE/BAYES/ADAPTIVE improve T1 relative losses by 0.02-0.23% only; DM/C2 detects the tiny consistent improvement (raw p = 0.0) but C1 remains the binding gate",
  "T2 h=0 CRPS relative loss ~0.89 for the control ensembles is driven by the SPF member that enters the candidate at 40/52 survey-deadline origins and is NOT part of the comparator; without SPF the equal ensemble is the comparator (relative loss 1.0)",
  "T2 h=0 RMSE is ~1.0 (no point-forecast improvement); C1 for T2 fails on RMSE",
  "ENSEMBLE_RW_AR cannot be evaluated on T2 (its RW member has no T2 model): zero forecasts, skipped; the T2 registration of that candidate is inconsistent"
 ],
